                <pb facs="0993" n="873" xml:id="pg873"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Graves to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I have been
                    informed by the minister of foreign affairs of Norway at Christiania that the
                    plebiscite held on the 12th and 13th of November, 1905, relative to the question
                    of form of government of Norway, had resulted in 259,563 votes in favor of a
                    monarchy and the election of His Highness Prince Charles of Denmark as King of
                    Norway, and 69,264 votes in favor of a republic.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles H.
                    Graves.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
